<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n30074" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Mursa</span></b>  or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Mursĭa</span></b> , ae, f., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a city in
			Pannonia</i>, now <i>Esgek</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Eutr. 9, 6</span></i>; <i><span class="en">10, 6</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">Aur.
				Vict. Epit. 41</span></i>.—Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Mursen-sis</span></b>  or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Mursĭensis</span></b> ,
			e, <i>adj., of</i> or <i>belonging to Mursa</i> or <i>Mursia,
			Mursian</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Mursense proelium,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Amm. 15, 5, 33</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">episcopus (al. Mursiensis),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hier. adv. Lucifer. 18</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Mursīnus</span></b> , a,
				um, <i>adj., of</i> or <i>belonging to the city of Mursa, Mursian</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">labes,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Aur.
					Vict. Caesar. 33</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
